  "note": "Drafted for Psalm 37 coverage.\n\nAdded 2026-11-21: לִוְיָתָן, from its former one-word entry. Filed under לוה 'twist, wind' with לִוְיָה 'wreath' (Pro 1:9), as the 'twisting serpent' (Isa 27:1) formed with ־ָן; Arabic لَوَى 'twist' (Lane p. 3015) and Ugaritic ltn 'the serpent' agree. The meaning differs from לוה 'join, borrow' in the same entry.\n\nIts former note: Ugaritic ltn is called a fleeing serpent in a parallel phrase to Isa 27:1. The full Hebrew noun supplies the key. A derivation from לוה is uncertain.",
